Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:03.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What if the Sun never stopped shining?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.29,0:00:04.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.14,0:00:07.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}You stand on a beach at noon.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.15,0:00:08.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The light never fades.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.98,0:00:10.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No sunset.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.10,0:00:11.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No twilight.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.23,0:00:12.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No night.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.24,0:00:13.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Ever.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.04,0:00:15.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.76,0:00:17.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.06,0:00:18.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The temperature climbs.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.69,0:00:19.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No cooling.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.94,0:00:21.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.35,0:00:23.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Forty degrees Celsius.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.16,0:00:24.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.98,0:00:27.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Plants photosynthesize nonstop.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.74,0:00:29.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}They burn through their water.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.54,0:00:30.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one week.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.85,0:00:32.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Forests turn brown.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.79,0:00:35.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Crops wither in fields.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.54,0:00:36.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one month.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.89,0:00:38.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Oceans steam.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.28,0:00:40.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Humidity becomes unbearable.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.80,0:00:42.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Rain never falls.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.37,0:00:44.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The water cycle breaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.86,0:00:46.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}After one year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.29,0:00:47.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The land is dust.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.85,0:00:50.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}No soil life remains.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.06,0:00:51.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}The poles melt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.48,0:00:54.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Sea levels rise sixty meters.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.88,0:00:56.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.61,0:00:58.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Earth already has a place like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.92,0:00:59.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Venus.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.96,0:01:04.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Its day lasts five thousand eight hundred thirty-two hours.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.09,0:01:08.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Surface temperature four hundred sixty-two degrees Celsius.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.53,0:01:09.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.68,0:01:11.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Night isn't darkness.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.52,0:01:12.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It's survival.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.87,0:01:15.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Would you miss the stars?
